#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Debugging and tracing {#debugging-and-tracing}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The "
"[`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build"
" \"samplomatic.build\") function transforms an annotated circuit into a "
"template circuit and samplex pair. In a complex circuit it can be hard to "
"tell which box in the original circuit corresponds to which barriers in the "
"template, or which nodes in the samplex DAG.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic provides two complementary tracing tools:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Barrier labels**: Every barrier in the template circuit carries a label "
"that encodes its origin. These are always present regardless of whether "
"`debug=True` is set.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Trace info on samplex nodes**: When "
"[`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build"
" \"samplomatic.build\") is called with `debug=True`, every samplex node "
"carries a `TraceInfo` object linking it back to the box or boxes that "
"produced it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both tools are most useful when boxes carry a "
"[`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag"
" \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation, which attaches a `ref` string to the box. "
"Alternatively, "
"[`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-"
"noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") references are "
"also attached.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tag boxes {#tag-boxes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A "
"[`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag"
" \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation attaches a `ref` string to a box. The `ref`"
" then appears in barrier labels and in trace information on samplex nodes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following example circuit has three boxes: two tagged CX boxes on "
"disjoint qubit pairs, and an untagged right-dressed measurement box. The "
"second CX box also carries an "
"[`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-"
"noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation — both"
" its `tag` ref and its noise `ref` will appear in the barrier labels. The "
"two CX boxes cover different qubits, which enables the samplex optimizer to "
"merge their propagation nodes into shared nodes. This is shown in the trace "
"information section.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Barrier labels in the template circuit {#barrier-labels-in-the-template-"
"circuit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calling "
"[`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build"
" \"samplomatic.build\") on the circuit above produces a template whose "
"barriers carry identifying labels. Each label has the form "
"`{side}{scope}@{key=value&...}`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Side**: `L` = left-dressing boundary, `M` = inner box content boundary, "
"`R` = right-dressing boundary.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Scope**: An integer index (or underscore-separated list for nested boxes) "
"that distinguishes multiple boxes at the same nesting level.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Annotations**: An `@`-prefixed, `&`-separated list of `key=value` pairs "
"derived from the box’s annotations. The `tag` key comes from a "
"[`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag"
" \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation and `inject_noise` comes from an "
"[`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-"
"noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Barriers from untagged boxes carry only the side and scope (for example, "
"`L2`), with no `@` suffix.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![../\\_images/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The barrier labels can also be extracted programmatically:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Trace information on samplex nodes {#trace-information-on-samplex-nodes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Passing `debug=True` to "
"[`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build"
" \"samplomatic.build\") attaches trace information to every samplex node. "
"Each node’s "
"[`trace_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-"
"nodes-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info "
"\"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info\") attribute is a `TraceInfo` "
"object whose `trace_refs` dictionary maps annotation keys (for example, "
"`\"tag\"` and `\"inject_noise\"`) to sets of ref strings. Nodes without a "
"corresponding box annotation have `trace_info=None`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-"
"samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw "
"\"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw\") is called on a debug-built samplex, "
"hovering over any node in the interactive graph reveals its `trace_refs` "
"inside the hover tooltip.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Trace information can also be inspected programmatically. Notice that some "
"nodes carry references from both `'cx_ab'` and `'cx_cd'`. The samplex "
"optimizer merged their parallel propagation nodes because the two boxes "
"cover disjoint qubits and share a common predecessor from the right-dressed "
"measurement box’s emission.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To find all nodes that originate from a specific box, filter by the "
"`\"tag\"` key:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The samplex DAG {#the-samplex-dag}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The samplex returned by "
"[`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build"
" \"samplomatic.build\") is a directed acyclic graph (DAG) where **edges "
"denote register dependency**. That is, an edge from node A to node B means B"
" must wait for A to have acted on the shared virtual registers before B is "
"allowed to act. This is not a temporal ordering like the DAG of a quantum "
"circuit. Instead, the graph flows from nodes responsible for generating "
"randomizations to nodes responsible for synthesizing them as outputs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are three node types, each with a distinct visual style in the "
"interactive plot:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Shape  | Color         | Type                                                                                                                                                             | Role                                                            |\n"
"| ------ | ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Star   | Red           | [`SamplingNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-sampling-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode\")         | Instantiates new virtual registers from a distribution or input |\n"
"| Circle | Green         | [`EvaluationNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-evaluation-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode\") | Transforms, combines, or propagates virtual registers           |\n"
"| Bowtie | Blue / Purple | [`CollectionNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collection-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode\") | Reads registers and writes to `sample()` outputs                |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execution proceeds in three phases:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "All sampling nodes run first (in parallel).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Evaluation nodes run next, in topological order (parallel within each "
"generation).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Collection nodes run last (in parallel).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The graphviz layout reflects this. Sampling nodes appear at the top, "
"collection nodes at the bottom.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hover tooltips {#hover-tooltips}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every node in the interactive visualization shows a tooltip when you hover "
"over it. The tooltip contains the following information:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Node class name** and its integer graph index.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Register manifests**, which registers the node instantiates, reads from, "
"writes to, and removes. These tell you how data flows between nodes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Node-specific details**, including the distribution type for sampling "
"nodes, the operand for multiplication nodes, the template parameter indices "
"for collection nodes, and so on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Trace refs** (only when `debug=True`), which are the annotation keys and "
"ref strings that link the node back to its originating boxes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Clicking the plot and then hovering over individual nodes is the fastest way"
" to understand what a given node does without reading source code.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Samplex summary {#samplex-summary}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before examining the visualization, `print(samplex)` gives a quick text "
"summary of the node count, required inputs, and promised outputs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect registers {#inspect-registers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Passing `keep_registers=True` to "
"[`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-"
"samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample "
"\"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") retains the intermediate "
"[`VirtualRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-"
"registers-virtual-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister "
"\"samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister\") objects that are live at "
"the end of sampling, and stores them in `outputs.metadata[\"registers\"]`. "
"Each register is a 2D array (shape `(num_subsystems, num_randomizations)`, "
"with possible trailing gate-shape dimensions) of virtual group elements.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is useful for verifying that virtual gates were combined correctly, or "
"for inspecting the raw Pauli or unitary samples before they are synthesized "
"into rotation angles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can view the contents of the end-state of a particular register. In the "
"following example, the register has type "
"[`PauliRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-"
"registers-pauli-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister "
"\"samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister\"). See the `API "
"documentation(/apidocs/index)`\\_\\_ for details about the storage format.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How samplex nodes map to template parameters {#how-samplex-nodes-map-to-"
"template-parameters}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `outputs[\"parameter_values\"]` array returned by "
"[`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-"
"samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample "
"\"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") has shape `(num_randomizations, N)`,"
" where `N` matches `len(template.parameters)`. Each column corresponds to "
"one parameter in the template circuit — the i-th column fills in "
"`template.parameters[i]`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The "
"[`CollectTemplateValues`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-"
"nodes-collect-template-"
"values#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues "
"\"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues\") collection nodes are "
"the link between virtual registers and template parameters. Each such node "
"holds index information that records which columns of the output array it "
"writes to. This makes it possible to trace which virtual gate subsystems "
"drive which template parameters.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See the \\{Samplex inputs and outputs}`samplex-io` guide to learn how to "
"bind the sampled parameter values to the template circuit and run "
"experiments.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Automatic tagging {#automatic-tagging}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When using "
"[`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-"
"generate-boxing-pass-"
"manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager "
"\"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\"), the `add_tags` "
"parameter automatically adds "
"[`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag"
" \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotations to all boxes. Three modes are available:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`\"unique_instance\"`**: Assigns sequential `ref` (`t0`, `t1`, and so on) "
"to boxes in circuit order. Every box gets a distinct `ref` regardless of its"
" structure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`\"unique_box\"`**: Computes a structural hash of each box’s content and "
"assigns the same `ref` to all structurally equivalent boxes. This is useful "
"for grouping boxes by type rather than position.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`\"noise_ref\"`**: Copies the `ref` from each box’s "
"[`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-"
"noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation and "
"only tags boxes that have one. This is useful when meaningful noise refs "
"already exist.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following example applies `\"unique_instance\"` and `\"unique_box\"` to "
"a circuit whose two CX boxes are structurally equivalent. With "
"`\"unique_instance\"`, each gets a distinct `ref`, while with "
"`\"unique_box\"`, they share one.\n"
msgstr ""
